At myPOS , we’re all about helping businesses grow and get paid. We make payments simple, smart, and accessible for everyone, but we’re more than just payment solutions - myPOS is a partner in growth. From free multicurrency accounts to powerful e-commerce tools, we’re here to support business owners of all sizes and everyone out there who dreams of starting their own business.
As we are expanding our team, we’re looking for Partner Relationships Manager to help us make a real difference in the Fintech industry. Ready to join us and shape the future of payments? Let’s make it happen!
About the role:
As we move into our next phase of growth, we’re on the lookout for Partner Relationships Managers to build, develop and scale high-performing partnerships across our key markets in Europe.
In this role, you will be the commercial owner and trusted relationship lead for a portfolio of strategic partners, helping them turn the myPOS proposition into sustainable merchant acquisition, transaction volume and revenue growth, and act as a key link between local stakeholders and central teams.
This position owns partnerships inSwitzerland, requiring a strong understanding of local partner ecosystems and go-to-market models.
What you’ll do:

• Own and develop a portfolio of strategic partners in Switzerland (e.g. ISVs, SaaS platforms, marketplaces, resellers, commerce and technology partners);

• Acting as their primary commercial contact and trusted day-to-day relationship manager, building long-term, trusted relationships;

• Drive partner activation from signed agreement to sustainable commercial performance, ensuring that partners are fully onboarded, trained, sales-ready and actively bringing myPOS to market;

• Identify and unlock growth opportunities across the existing partner base, including new merchant segments, verticals, regions, sales channels, product adoption opportunities and cross-sell potential;

• Help partners define and execute effective go-to-market motions for myPOS , including reseller models, referral programmes, bundled offerings, merchant migration campaigns, vertical-specific propositions and joint customer-acquisition activities;

• Coordinate with Marketing on co-marketing campaigns, partner communications, case studies, events, webinars, lead-generation initiatives and sales collateral that help partners acquire merchants;

• Monitor local market trends, partner performance, and competitive landscape.

This role is perfect for you if you have:

• 5+ years of experience in relationship management, business development, or strategic alliances;

• Proven experience working with technology, SaaS, platform, or reseller partners;

• Understanding of APIs, integrations, or partner-led growth models;

• Strong commercial mindset and negotiation skills;

• Ability to work cross-functionally in an international environment;

• Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills;

• Analytical and data-driven approach to performance tracking;

• Fluent in English and applicable local language(s).

Who we are:
Since 2014 we’ve been all about making payments easier and more accessible for businesses of all shapes and sizes. Whether you’re at the counter, selling online, or on the move, we’ve got businesses covered with smart, accessible and affordable solutions that keep things easy.
Our mission? It’s simple. Help businesses get paid by taking advantage of modern tech and innovative ideas, so payment challenges are a thing of the past.
Pro tip:
Take it easy about meeting every requirement - this job description is just that, a job description! Even if you don’t tick every box, want you to apply anyway! This is your chance to grow, learn, and build your career with us. We value potential over perfection, and we are all about mutual growth!
Apply by filling in the form below and send your CV in English!
